WEBVTT

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.820
These shoulders just won't quit aching.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.740
You <i>have</i> been pretty busy lately.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.330
I sure could use a trip to a hot spring.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.870
I know what you mean. We could go to Kiyo or North Makinata...

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.290
It's such a long trip, though.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.510
That's so close!

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.550
What is?

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.470
Hot spring! A hot spring!
This article says one was built close by!

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.390
Say what?!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.220
They're getting the water from Mt. Konuta.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.310
Now that I think about it, they've been building something for a while.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.890
What kind of hot spring is it?

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.480
Let's see...

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.360
It says there's a rocky bath fed by a stream of hot spring water,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:52.030
where you can enjoy cold sake served in Konuta earthenware,

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.280
and when you return to your room, a little tipsy, you can have knotweed sweetfish and uruka...

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.620
Oh, you can stay overnight there!

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.540
That sounds great... That sounds really great!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.710
Let's head over there right now, Mikochi!

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.330
Hang on! We need to pack a change of clothes!

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.260
I sincerely apologize for this.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:51.980
A group of our feline guests has clogged the drains with their shedding.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.270
So right now it's all...

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.780
...being cleaned?

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.070
If it's a meal and lodging you're after, we can still...

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.070
Oh, no thanks.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.490
We'll come back some other time.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.420
What do we do now?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.420
I don't think there's anything that can fill this void.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:29.390
I bet all this bamboo looks really pretty from an outdoor bath.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.140
I bet it does...

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.520
Want to plant some bamboo around the house?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.450
Right, let's build one.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.860
One what?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.950
An outdoor bath!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.740
What? Can you make those?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.830
No idea. I've never tried.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.330
A rock-lined bath doesn't seem too complicated.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.120
A rock bath, huh?

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.340
Laying the foundation and sealing it up would take a few days, though.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.710
How about using wood? Would cypress work?

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:03.840
Piecing together something waterproof is tricky.
Hollowing out a big chunk wouldn't be easy, either.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.510
I wonder if there's some good raw material around here...

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.610
Bamboo!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.730
Oh!

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:20.690
A "bamboo pipe bath" type thing, right?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.530
No—you'd need a seriously big piece of bamboo for that.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.820
I'll split it in half to make the bath.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.580
Like for somen noodles, right?
But won't it be hard to cut down the bamboo?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.750
If it's the whole bamboo stalk, yeah.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.500
If it's just the base, I can manage.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.960
Let's go find someone who'll lend us a saw.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.430
Oh! I knew we'd find one.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.180
A leftover stump.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.600
Why did they leave such a random height of stalk behind?

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.520
When you're cutting bamboo this big,
you ask someone really tall to do it for you.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:01.940
That's why this much is left. Looks like someone around the vice president's size did this one.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.320
Makes sense.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.780
Now let's get cutting.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.530
Nothing like a workout before taking a bath, I guess.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:18.290
First, we make a diagonal notch with the hatchet and saw horizontally.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.670
I need you to copy me, Mikochi.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.550
Okay, got it.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.970
With a stump this small, it shouldn't really matter where we start cutting.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.560
Hm? What do you mean?

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:39.060
If you cut on just one side of a grown bamboo stalk,
it'll split under its own weight and spring your way.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.570
What?

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:43.530
It'll have a huge amount of force behind it, too.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.860
You'd get hurt real bad in the <i>best</i> case.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.450
You're sure about this, right?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.160
All right. That should do it.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.580
Mikochi, move back a little bit.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.310
Hakumei?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.730
Still standing, are you?

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.440
Mikochi, let's combine our strength!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.110
Huh? You want me to jump, too?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.580
Great! That did the trick.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:44.550
Ouch... How exactly are we going to get this home?

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.880
We'll roll it!

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.940
So we went to a hot spring and your shoulders got even <i>more</i> stiff?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.320
I guess so.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:09.150
What kind of sake do you want? Ginjo, Junmai, or...

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.320
We have some Kuragakoi, right?
Let's pop that one open.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:32.220
We need to drop some hot stones into a bamboo cylinder I submerged earlier.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.600
It's like nabe.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.810
That looks great.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.230
The temperature should be about right, now.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.780
Hey, what about the screen?

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.990
Oh, I forgot!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.460
This feels divine...

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.840
Yeah...

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.850
Well, I guess that proves you can build your own outdoor bath.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.720
You did a great job. Why not have a drink?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.470
What do we have to munch on?

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.560
Roasted, salted squid.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.650
Also, seaweed stems and okra, with sesame sauce.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.440
I made the flavors quite rich, to go with the Kuragakoi.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.990
Nice.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.910
I want to go to sleep right here, just like this.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.160
Maybe if we didn't have to keep dropping in hot stones...

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.460
Let's make a reservation at that hot spring after all, sometime.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.970
Yeah. And steal their way of making rock baths.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.320
There was nothing but food at the market this morning.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.150
Just the sight of it got my mouth watering...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.280
But we didn't buy any of it.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.160
We've got to save our money.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.740
There's still plenty of food at home.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.540
Delivery coming through!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.170
Wow... An entire daikon radish.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.930
How extravagant.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.600
I wonder if they'll be having an oden festival.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.060
That'd still be too much daikon.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.930
I wonder where he could be delivering...

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:48.190
Your signature here, please.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.940
Sure thing.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:53.190
Mi... ko... chi.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.030
How much was this, again?

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.950
2,500.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.240
Here. Exact change.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.280
So it is.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.450
Ayune?!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:08.920
Oh my. Welcome back, Mikochi.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.290
Who's this?

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.920
Wh... Why are you...

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.880
You must be Hakumei-chan.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.430
"-chan"?! Yeah, I am...

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:27.180
Thank you for taking such good care of my sister.
I'm Mikochi's older sister, Ayune.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.990
You don't really look alike.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.660
Oh, really?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.790
Why did you come here?

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.330
To see you.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.500
Heave ho.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.080
Always a pleasure!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.630
Hey, what's that daikon for?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.800
Oh, they were selling it in town. Think of it as a gift.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.550
Oh, okay then.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.770
Well, isn't this a nice place.
Would you call it folkloric, perhaps?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.480
What the heck is that?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.770
Here's some coffee.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.940
Thanks.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.530
How's Makinata working out for you?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.490
It's nice, if a little expensive.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.280
And how's it going back home?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.780
The same as always.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:27.120
It's a bit lonely without you around, though.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.580
Now that doesn't sound like anything you'd ever say.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.000
It doesn't?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:37.250
Since you left, I've started spending a lot of time reminiscing.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.130
Uh... You have?

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:47.310
I'm sorry, Hakumei-chan. I've made you listen to such boring talk.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.270
Oh, no...

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:54.150
I hate to say this, since maybe you're only trying to be considerate of me. But Ayune...

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.400
Hm?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.900
Are you just putting on an act?

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.990
She's a sharp one. I can't believe I've already been found out.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:12.080
I wanted to try playing the
"good older sister" role. How'd I do?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.130
So saying you came to see me was...

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.380
A lie.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.250
Of course it was.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:23.050
I'm sorry, Hakumei-chan. Were you surprised?

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:26.300
I'm meeting you for the first time, so why would I be?

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.720
So, what do you want?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:33.060
I've got a touch of writer's block.
I needed a change in scenery.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.230
Might you perhaps let me know before coming?

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.690
Nah, that'd just be a pain.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.320
It's not like it's any real bother to you if your sister happens to show up on your doorstep.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.160
It's a nuisance! I'm not a child anymore, you know!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.950
I've got a job. And a life!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.790
You're always so self-centered.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.490
Delivery!
You're always so self-centered.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.450
Delivery!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:56.080
Oh, I also bought seasoning for stewed daikon.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.540
Presents, lots of presents!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.840
Just leave!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.090
Umm...

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.840
It's fine. You don't have to worry about being nice.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.430
She's an interesting one.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.890
That's not the word I would use.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.860
Ayune works as a playwright.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.610
It tore. Fix it.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.070
But she won't lift a finger aside from that.
It tore. Fix it.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.400
What, again?
But she won't lift a finger aside from that.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.660
Why did you just decide to clean up my room?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.490
She won't do chores or cooking,
nor give a thought to budgeting.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.830
Because you won't ever clean.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.580
What did you buy this time?

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.250
And yet she's so very arrogant...
What did you buy this time?

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.790
It's a model of a turtle shell. It's made of pure silver.
And yet she's so very arrogant...

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:37.370
It's a model of a turtle shell. It's made of pure silver.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:43.380
My cooking skill and sense of self-reliance were cultivated in those days.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.640
What kind of plays does Ayune write?
Are they fun to watch?

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:54.730
Yeah.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:14:00.440
They're <i>really</i> fun to watch!
And that's what's so frustrating!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.730
Oh...

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.150
Mikochi, look!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.400
Check it out.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.990
Soy sauce.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.280
You want me to cook with nothing but soy sauce?

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.540
What am I supposed to do with all this?!
We don't need a whole daikon, either!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.540
But they were selling the whole thing.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.670
Couldn't you have asked them to cut it?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.250
Daikon doesn't keep very long!

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.800
Now, now...

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.340
If we cut and dry it, it should last for a while.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.340
You've got a good head on your shoulders, Hakumei-chan!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.890
You do know that you've got to help out, right, Ayune?

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.100
That's a lousy way to treat a guest.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.150
Is this your way of peeling daikon?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.820
It sure is.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.910
And you can't slice it up thin either, huh?

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.710
My success rate is around thirty percent, I suppose.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.800
You're as handy as always.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.050
Do you still make clothes as well?

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.050
On occasion. I had a part-time job as a dressmaker, too.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.310
Maybe I'll order some costumes for the troupe from you someday.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.850
Well...

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.810
I wouldn't really mind doing—

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.570
Hey, hey, Hakumei-chan!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.990
Got any good stories to tell me?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.530
Good stories, huh?

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.160
I've got stories from when I was traveling...

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.620
Or for something more recent, maybe about that time we saw the evening kite.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.830
You mean the legendary red bird?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.420
Turns out that was Kafu the whole time.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.340
What? Wasn't he white, though?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.800
He soaks up the red of the sunset.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.850
When he bathes in the morning sun,
he turns white again.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.770
I'm not kidding, you know. He really does—

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:08.280
It's no use talking to her now.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.110
Huh?

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:13.910
"The bird who grants wishes..."

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.530
"absorbs the deep red of evening..."

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.040
"...bright sunlight wipes his wings clean."

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:26.750
When she gets like this, she'll be a brick wall until she finally says "I'm hungry."

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.800
She's a tough sister to deal with, isn't she...

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.610
I came here just so that I could eat this.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.940
What about your writer's block?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.910
That was a lie. The reason I just gave is a lie too.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.410
What's the real reason, then?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.990
Isn't it obvious?

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.580
To see my dear little sis—

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.290
Lies.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.710
You've got a heart of ice.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.960
She was such a sweet child when we were young, too...

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:07.790
Wha...

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.510
Hakumei-chan, do you want to hear an old story about Mikochi?

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:12.300
Stop it!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.930
"Onee-chan, I wrote a story, too."

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.840
Stop!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.800
"You're in it too!"

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.720
I'm telling you to stop!

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.100
But we're just getting to the fun part!

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.560
Just cut it out.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.600
I bet you bully Haruka the same way, don't you?

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:30.570
No way. I wouldn't dream of tormenting my dear little brother!

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:33.650
You haven't changed one bit, have you?

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:34.950
Look who's talking.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:37.200
And you still hold chopsticks like a kid!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.330
Nice technique, huh? I can even hold tofu like this.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.740
You two.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.290
Eat it while it's still hot.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:49.540
That's the bare minimum of respect that you should be showing this stewed daikon.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:52.670
Huh?

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:54.720
Eat up before it gets cold!

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.220
Yes ma'am!

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.760
She reminds me of Dad.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.220
Be quiet and eat.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.530
Hakumei-chan takes long baths, huh?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.530
She's just being considerate.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.110
Yeah, I know.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.120
You like whiskey, right?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.870
Yeah.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.880
Hey. Why did you really come here?

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.760
Every reason I gave... They were all true.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:36.970
More lies, huh?

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:38.760
It's the honest truth this time.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:43.390
I had writer's block, and I wanted to eat stewed daikon with miso.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.810
And what about wanting to see me?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.810
I really did.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.400
I got a bit sad thinking that I hadn't seen you in so long.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:03.910
That's not true. I know there's no way <i>you'd</i> ever feel lonely.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:10.210
Even when you were struggling with your writing alone,
you never looked the least bit depressed.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.420
I guess that's how it must have looked.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.970
What do you mean?

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.600
Oh, who knows.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:31.600
You could just stop if you don't enjoy it anymore.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.560
Yeah.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:37.940
Don't make that face. You'll make me worry.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.950
Right. Sorry.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.410
But you know, that Hakumei-chan...

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.620
I've got to hand it to her.
Putting up with you this whole time.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.700
What's that supposed to mean?

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.420
Let me guess. You captured her heart with your cooking.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:58.050
I should get you to teach me how to cook before I leave.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.670
It'd take you a good six months to learn.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.800
Well, that's not really an option for me.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.720
I'm going to head out.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.600
What? Now?

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:11.940
Hakumei-chan, you can come out now!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.560
Huh?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.860
You come and go so suddenly...

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.070
If you give me a tearful plea,
I can stay a little bit longer.

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.700
I refuse.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.700
Gosh, you're such a cold-hearted little sister.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:27.830
Well, then.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.080
See you, Mikochi.

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.600
Onee-chan...

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:47.850
Yeah.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.970
Are you going to quit writing?!

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:51.350
What?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.270
That's your first question?

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.940
Well, we were just talking about it earlier...

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.520
You're getting married?

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.860
Yes. To a member of the theater troupe.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.490
So, Mikochi. What should I do?

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:07.030
I could go either way, personally.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.000
Don't you dare quit!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.000
Okay, I won't.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.000
Absolutely not, okay?

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:26.840
Congratulations, Ayune.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.430
Thank you, Mikochi.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.560
Take care of yourselves!

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:43.150
Now that I think about it, she didn't give us his name or tell us anything about the wedding.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.700
Wait, Ayune!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.580
You forgot the most important part!

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.540
Is it me, or is she running away?

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.920
Well, I'm sure we can expect a letter, right?

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.000
Good grief...

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.920
If you're still in the mood to drink, I'll join you.

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:08.590
It's fine. I'll have a drink alone.

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.260
Okay, got it.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.970
Good night.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.230
Good night.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:35.410
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:43.210
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:47.220
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:51.180
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:55.720
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:00.100
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:03.730
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:07.440
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.410
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:16.200
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:20.170
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:24.130
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:29.420
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:32.970
At least, that's how we're feeling
